    {
      "id": "e291",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1162,
      "y": 1223,
      "width": 786,
      "height": 26.25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786374270278,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A single 2U server on extended rails, out of a lightly loaded rack, will tip it. Fit the stabilizer foot or anchor the rack to the slab BEFORE the first\ninstall, not after the room is full. Load heaviest at the bottom and work up - which is also why the UPS sits at U1-U6 on T-201.",
      "originalText": "A single 2U server on extended rails, out of a lightly loaded rack, will tip it. Fit the stabilizer foot or anchor the rack to the slab BEFORE the first\ninstall, not after the room is full. Load heaviest at the bottom and work up - which is also why the UPS sits at U1-U6 on T-201.",
